// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 16 „B2 grammatika integratsioon” (b1b2-076…080), stage B2.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md), January–February, before Sofia's B2 exam (7 March) and before the café opens (18 April). Three
// people edit three texts. Tuul Logistika has tested a temporary warehouse in Ülenurme near Tartu since August; in early
// March the board decides whether a permanent warehouse opens there in May. Liis asked Sofia to edit the pilot's final
// report by the end of February; trainee Laura (until the end of February) wrote the draft (true facts, choppy
// sentences). Jaan and Kadri prepare the family café „Kohvik Mets” next to Nõmme market (opens 18 April; the name = the
// family name and Viktor's forest farm, where the bread recipe comes from; Muki is still the dog). A tasting evening for
// the neighbours in the unfinished café in February; Jaan writes „Meie lugu” and the house rules, Kadri edits them.
// Helgi proofreads by video call Oskar's (5.b) story for the school paper „Kase Kaja” (editor: class teacher Kristel
// Saar) about baking rye bread at Viktor's farm in January. One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner
// edits a real document together with its author (Sofia's report summary, 079 Kasuta) and writes its final version.
// Grammar (B2 integration, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): complex sentences and connectors (kuigi, ehkki, samal ajal
// kui, seetõttu, mistõttu, juhul kui) with the verb after them in 076; word order — verb second, a main clause after a
// subordinate one starts with the verb, given → new information, existential sentences with a partial subject, -ki/-gi
// (keegi, ükski, kunagi, isegi …-gi) in 077; participles -v / -tav / -nud / -tud as attributes, the des-form and
// nominalisation -mine / -ja (grammarPlan „nonfinite”) in 078; mood by function — impersonal for rules, conditional for
// requests and proposals, quotative for unchecked claims — and the government of official verbs (pöörduma kelle poole,
// nõustuma millega, sõltuma millest, vastutama mille eest) in 079. Spiral: essive (projektijuhina, esindajana), translative
// (muutus tasuliseks, saada tõlkijaks), total vs partial object and subject (paigaldasid riiuleid / riiulid; Menüüs on
// suppe), all of them again in the final summary (079 Kasuta).
// The final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 16, 2026-10-29): 076 PROJ L→S (corner L2 = the radio interview
// „Päevateema” with Sofia and Ilze Berg, ten questions with three options; main = S16 Sofia's talk at the board meeting,
// recorded at home), 077 KIRJ L→W (corner L4 = the talk show „Kas hea tekst müüb?”, twelve true / false statements; main
// = W14 argument „Kas keelt saab õppida ilma kursuseta?” for the library's website), 078 RÄÄK R→S (corner S2 = argument
// cards: does the café bake its own bread or buy it, S17; main = S16 the bread video for the café's site, recorded at
// home), 079 LUGE R→W (corner R3 = the report chapter on the paid car park, twelve gaps with four options; main = W15 the
// report summary with the chart and a comment). Every teaching lesson: review naming the previous lesson and a module
// 12–14 lesson, a pair task in the lesson, a home recording in Kasuta (S16 / S15), two fluency tasks; S16 in 076 and 078,
// S17 in 076 and 078.
//   076 the project meeting (gaps); the radio interview; Laura's introduction with a connector bank; Sofia's mail to Liis;
//       Kasuta: the board meeting and Liis's offer to Markus — argument cards, Sofia's talk, Markus's reply.
//   077 Jaan reads his draft to Kadri (short answers); the talk show; Henri Pärtel's news item (sentence bank); Kasuta: the
//       library's language café — three guests' stories, the interview, a home recording, the argument for the website.
//   078 Oskar's story „Kuidas sünnib rukkileib”; Helgi and Oskar edit it by video call; the school paper's notice; bake or
//       buy (argument cards); Kasuta: Viktor's recipe cards, Jaan and Pille in the kitchen, the video, the kitchen guide.
//   079 the café's house rules after the tasting evening (four voices); the report chapter on the paid car park; colleagues'
//       voice messages; Kasuta: the module project — editor and author edit Laura's summary, the final version.
// Lesson 5 (080) is Vahehindamine 4, a full mock in Harno B2 form: listening L1, L2, L3, L4; reading R1, R2a, R2b, R3, R4;
// writing W1, W2b; speaking S1, S2; every part timed with B.examPart. The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module16.js.
